      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under aerobic conditions, to a stirred colorless solution of dapdoH2 (0.04 g, 0.2 mmol) and NEt3 (0.14 mL, 1.0 mmol) in MeOH/H2O (20 mL, 10:1 v/v) were added solids Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (0.27 g, 0.6 mmol) and Cu(NO3)2·3H2O (0.05 g, 0.2 mmol) together (main-text molar ratio Cu:Ln:dapdoH2:Me3SiN3:NEt3 = 1:3:1:3:5). The pale blue suspension was stirred for 30 min while Me3SiN3 (0.08 mL, 0.6 mmol) was added in portions, giving a deep blue solution. The solution was filtered and the filtrate was allowed to evaporate slowly at room temperature. After 5 days, X-ray quality blue crystals of 1 were collected by filtration, washed with cold MeOH (2 × 3 mL), and dried in air. The solid was analyzed as 1·4H2O.",
        "reagents": [
